## ops.sh Remote Operations

<!-- Remove if not using ops.sh -->

**All remote interaction goes through `./ops.sh`.** No direct SSH, docker exec, or raw SQL — ever.

```bash
./ops.sh help | deploy | logs backend | status | health | db backup
```

**Safety tiers:** SAFE (logs/status/health) → MODERATE (deploy/restart, needs confirm) → HUMAN_REQUIRED (rollback/restore) → BLOCKED (DROP/TRUNCATE/DELETE)

